    "result_text": "The build is green. There's a single test class in the project, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the welcome notification on successful owner creation.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java`: a one-method OfficeFloor step that reads the persisted `Owner` via `@Val` and emits a line to the `NOTIFY` logger containing the owner id and `memberId`:\n\n```java\nNOTIFY.info(\"welcome: id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n```\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted a `notify` step between `audit` and `respond`. It runs only on the successful-create path (after `save`, which assigns the id, and `assignMemberId`, which sets the `memberId`), and carries `govern: [ transaction ]` consistent with the surrounding steps.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` test \u2014 which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both the owner id and the fetched `memberId` \u2014 passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
